& [PreservedDirection]
  + continue the active twelve-hour productization goal through the next dependency-contiguous existing product seam rather than invent unrelated features
  + the published portable-bundle reentry selects a provider-free operator configuration profile with redacted diagnostics and no production secret material

& [Situation]
  + cantord already has exact strict service-config token activation signed-environment and prepared-runtime validators
  + today the only exact way to exercise their complete chain is to attempt server startup and listener binding
  + operators lack a deterministic no-listener machine report that distinguishes readiness from a safe public refusal

& [Intent]
  + add one cantord check-config mode that reuses the existing validators without binding a listener or starting the service loop
  + return closed ordered stage results and safe configuration/runtime summary or one sanitized refusal
  + never serialize paths token bytes token hashes source content environment content or raw operating-system error messages

& [Boundaries]
  + validation may read the operator-selected config token activation and environment files exactly as normal startup already does
  + it creates no secret config activation environment state log process listener network request or provider contact
  + no migration repair mutation installer publisher trust supported delivery upgrade effect remote FPGA or Minecraft authority
